# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Onsite — frontend env (copy to .env.local for local overrides)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Backend API base URL. Leave EMPTY to keep the dev-friendly default (`/api`,
# resolved via the Vite proxy to localhost:3001). Set in production builds
# (e.g. via a GitHub Pages repo Variable) to point at your deployed backend.
# Example: https://readytoflutter-api.onrender.com/api
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Optional GitHub Pages fallback. If VITE_API_BASE_URL is unset and the page
# is served from *.github.io, the runtime falls back to this URL. Used so a
# fork deployed to Pages can still talk to a known backend without having to
# set VITE_API_BASE_URL explicitly. Leave empty to disable the fallback (the
# app keeps working in anonymous-only mode).
# VITE_PROD_API_FALLBACK_URL=https://readytoflutter.onrender.com/api

# Override the base path. Useful when deploying to a non-root path like
# /readytoflutter/. Auto-inferred from GITHUB_REPOSITORY in CI; you almost
# never need to set this manually.
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/readytoflutter/

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Analytics (optional — OFF by default)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WITH NEITHER KEY SET, THE APP RUNS WITH ANALYTICS DISABLED. No SDK is
# downloaded, no network request is made, nothing is stored. Events still log
# to the dev console via `console.debug('[analytics] …')`, so you can read the
# whole event stream locally without a provider account.
#
# To turn it on: pick AT MOST one provider below, uncomment its key, and
# restart the dev server (Vite only reads env at boot). Nothing else to do —
# every call site is already instrumented, so a key is the entire switch.
#
# Do Not Track is honoured: if the browser sends DNT, no provider is loaded
# for that visitor even when a key is configured.
#
# Events sent (see the `AnalyticsEvent` union in src/lib/analytics.ts, which is
# the authoritative list — the type makes a typo a build error):
#   account    signup_start · signup · login · logout · account_deleted
#   discovery  stack_selected · topic_opened · search
#   core       answer_revealed · bookmark_toggled ·
#              study_session_start/complete · mock_session_start · mock_complete ·
#              ai_grade_used
#   revenue    paywall_hit · upgrade_click
#   support    contact_submitted
# Plus one $pageview per route change (SPA pageviews are sent manually, so
# PostHog is initialised with capture_pageview:false — don't re-enable it or
# every navigation is counted twice).

# PostHog (free tier covers solo projects). Get a Project API Key from
# https://posthog.com/ → Project settings → Project API Key. It is a public,
# write-only key: shipping it in the client bundle is expected.
# VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# Host defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com. Change it for the EU cloud
# (https://eu.i.posthog.com) or a self-hosted instance.
# VITE_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Plausible (alternative to PostHog — privacy-first, no cookies, but only a
# handful of custom-property dimensions). Set the verified site domain you
# registered in Plausible. Ignored whenever VITE_POSTHOG_KEY is also set.
# VITE_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=onsite.example.com
